[2026-03-14T21:00:33.481Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TW8D5Kk1Cw3MQqHkeTerLv","type":"tool_result","content":"   935→### Component: AddListingForm\n   936→\n   937→#### Test: Clicking Add Listing button opens the multi-step form\n   938→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Listings tab.\n   939→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Add Listing\" button.\n   940→- **Expected:** A multi-step form opens (modal or full-page). Step 1 is displayed with fields for property type and title. A step indicator shows progress (Step 1 of 7). \"Next\" and \"Cancel\" buttons are visible.\n   941→\n   942→#### Test: Step 1 — Property type selection and title input\n   943→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is open on Step 1.\n   944→- **Expected:** A dropdown or selection control lists property types: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". A text input field for the property title is visible. Both fields are required.\n   945→\n   946→#### Test: Step 1 — Selecting property type and entering title\n   947→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 1.\n   948→- **Action:** User selects \"Cabin\" from the property type selector and types \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\" in the title field.\n   949→- **Expected:** The property type shows \"Cabin\" selected. The title field displays \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\". The \"Next\" button becomes enabled (or was already enabled).\n   950→\n   951→#### Test: Step 1 — Validation prevents proceeding without required fields\n   952→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 1 with no selections made.\n   953→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\" without selecting a property type or entering a title.\n   954→- **Expected:** Validation errors are displayed for both fields (e.g., \"Property type is required\", \"Title is required\"). The form does not advance to Step 2.\n   955→\n   956→#### Test: Step 2 — Location fields displayed\n   957→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 1 and clicked \"Next\".\n   958→- **Expected:** Step 2 is displayed with fields for: address (with geocoding/autocomplete), city, state, and country. A \"Back\" button and \"Next\" button are visible. The step indicator shows Step 2 of 7.\n   959→\n   960→#### Test: Step 2 — Address field uses autocomplete\n   961→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2.\n   962→- **Action:** User types \"123 Main\" in the address field.\n   963→- **Expected:** An autocomplete dropdown appears with address suggestions from a geocoding API (e.g., OpenStreetMap Nominatim). Selecting a suggestion populates the address field with the full address.\n   964→\n   965→#### Test: Step 2 — Address autocomplete populates related fields\n   966→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2.\n   967→- **Action:** User types in the address field and selects an autocomplete suggestion for \"123 Main St, Denver, CO, USA\".\n   968→- **Expected:** The address field is populated with \"123 Main St\". The city field is auto-filled with \"Denver\". The state field is auto-filled with \"CO\". The country field is auto-filled with \"USA\".\n   969→\n   970→#### Test: Step 2 — Validation requires city and country\n   971→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2 with address filled but city and country empty.\n   972→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n   973→- **Expected:** Validation errors appear for city and country (e.g., \"City is required\", \"Country is required\"). The form does not advance.\n   974→\n   975→#### Test: Step 3 — Details fields displayed\n   976→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 2 and clicked \"Next\".\n   977→- **Expected:** Step 3 is displayed with numeric input fields for: max guests, bedrooms, beds, and bathrooms. Each field has increment/decrement controls or is a number input. The step indicator shows Step 3 of 7.\n   978→\n   979→#### Test: Step 3 — Setting property details\n   980→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 3.\n   981→- **Action:** User sets max guests to 4, bedrooms to 2, beds to 3, bathrooms to 1.\n   982→- **Expected:** All fields display the entered values. The \"Next\" button is enabled.\n   983→\n   984→#### Test: Step 3 — Validation requires all detail fields\n   985→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 3 with all fields at 0 or empty.\n   986→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n   987→- **Expected:** Validation errors appear (e.g., \"Max guests must be at least 1\"). The form does not advance.\n   988→\n   989→#### Test: Step 4 — Amenities selection displayed\n   990→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 3 and clicked \"Next\".\n   991→- **Expected:** Step 4 is displayed with checkboxes for amenities grouped by category: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each category heading is visible with its amenities listed below. The step indicator shows Step 4 of 7.\n   992→\n   993→#### Test: Step 4 — Selecting amenities\n   994→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 4 with amenities loaded from `GET /api/amenities`.\n   995→- **Action:** User checks \"WiFi\" and \"Kitchen\" under Essentials, and \"Pool\" under Features.\n   996→- **Expected:** The selected amenities show as checked. The user can proceed to the next step. Amenities are optional (no validation error if none selected).\n   997→\n   998→#### Test: Step 4 — Amenities are toggleable\n   999→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 4 with \"WiFi\" already checked.\n  1000→- **Action:** User clicks \"WiFi\" to uncheck it, then checks it again.\n  1001→- **Expected:** The checkbox toggles correctly on each click.\n  1002→\n  1003→#### Test: Step 5 — Photo URL input displayed\n  1004→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 4 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1005→- **Expected:** Step 5 is displayed with an input field for image URLs and an \"Add Photo\" button. A list/grid of added photos is shown below (initially empty). The step indicator shows Step 5 of 7.\n  1006→\n  1007→#### Test: Step 5 — Adding a photo URL\n  1008→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5.\n  1009→- **Action:** User types \"https://example.com/photo1.jpg\" in the URL input and clicks \"Add Photo\".\n  1010→- **Expected:** The photo URL is added to the list. A preview or thumbnail of the image is displayed. The URL input is cleared for the next entry. An optional caption field may be shown for the added photo.\n  1011→\n  1012→#### Test: Step 5 — Adding multiple photo URLs\n  1013→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with one photo already added.\n  1014→- **Action:** User adds two more photo URLs.\n  1015→- **Expected:** All three photos are displayed in the list/grid. Each photo can be reordered or removed.\n  1016→\n  1017→#### Test: Step 5 — Removing a photo\n  1018→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with 3 photos added.\n  1019→- **Action:** User clicks the remove/delete button on the second photo.\n  1020→- **Expected:** The second photo is removed from the list. The remaining 2 photos are displayed.\n  1021→\n  1022→#### Test: Step 5 — Validation requires at least one photo\n  1023→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with no photos added.\n  1024→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n  1025→- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"At least one photo is required\"). The form does not advance.\n  1026→\n  1027→#### Test: Step 6 — Pricing fields displayed\n  1028→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 5 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1029→- **Expected:** Step 6 is displayed with numeric input fields for: price per night and cleaning fee. The price per night field is required. The cleaning fee defaults to 0. Currency formatting or prefix ($) is shown. The step indicator shows Step 6 of 7.\n  1030→\n  1031→#### Test: Step 6 — Entering pricing information\n  1032→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6.\n  1033→- **Action:** User enters 150 for price per night and 50 for cleaning fee.\n  1034→- **Expected:** The fields display $150 and $50 respectively.\n  1035→\n  1036→#### Test: Step 6 — Validation requires price per night\n  1037→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6 with price per night empty or 0.\n  1038→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n  1039→- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"Price per night is required and must be greater than 0\"). The form does not advance.\n  1040→\n  1041→#### Test: Step 7 — Review and publish page displayed\n  1042→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 6 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1043→- **Expected:** Step 7 displays a summary of all entered information: property type, title, full address (address, city, state, country), details (guests, bedrooms, beds, bathrooms), selected amenities, photo thumbnails, price per night, and cleaning fee. A \"Publish\" button and \"Back\" button are visible. The step indicator shows Step 7 of 7.\n  1044→\n  1045→#### Test: Step 7 — Review page shows all entered data correctly\n  1046→- **Initial state:** User has filled out all steps: type \"Cabin\", title \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\", address \"123 Pine Rd, Aspen, CO, USA\", 4 guests, 2 bedrooms, 2 beds, 1 bathroom, amenities \"WiFi\" and \"Kitchen\", 2 photos, price $200/night, cleaning fee $75.\n  1047→- **Expected:** The review page displays all of these values accurately. No data is missing or incorrect.\n  1048→\n  1049→#### Test: Publishing a new listing creates the property\n  1050→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 7 (Review) with all data entered correctly.\n  1051→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Publish\" button.\n  1052→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/properties` with the property data, then `POST /api/property-images` for each photo. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing published successfully!\"). The form closes. The new property appears in the Listings tab grid. The \"Total Listings\" stat increments by 1.\n  1053→\n  1054→#### Test: Back button navigates to the previous step\n  1055→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 3 of the Add Listing form.\n  1056→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Back\" button.\n  1057→- **Expected:** The form navigates to Step 2. All previously entered data in Step 2 is preserved (city, address, etc. are still filled).\n  1058→\n  1059→#### Test: Cancel button closes the form without saving\n  1060→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 4 of the Add Listing form with data entered in Steps 1–3.\n  1061→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button.\n  1062→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Discard your listing? All entered information will be lost.\" with \"Discard\" and \"Keep Editing\" buttons.\n  1063→\n  1064→#### Test: Confirming cancel discards the listing form\n  1065→- **Initial state:** The discard confirmation dialog is open.\n  1066→- **Action:** User clicks \"Discard\".\n  1067→- **Expected:** The form closes. No API calls are made. The user returns to the Listings tab. No new property is created.\n  1068→\n  1069→#### Test: Dismissing cancel keeps the form open\n  1070→- **Initial state:** The discard confirmation dialog is open.\n  1071→- **Action:** User clicks \"Keep Editing\".\n  1072→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The form remains on the current step with all data preserved.\n  1073→\n  1074→#### Test: Step indicator shows correct progress throughout the form\n  1075→- **Initial state:** User opens the Add Listing form.\n  1076→- **Action:** User navigates through all 7 steps using Next/Back buttons.\n  1077→- **Expected:** The step indicator accurately shows the current step (e.g., \"Step 1 of 7\", \"Step 2 of 7\", etc.) at each stage. Completed steps may show a checkmark or different styling.\n  1078→\n  1079→#### Test: Data persistence across steps when navigating back and forth\n  1080→- **Initial state:** User has filled out Steps 1–5 and is on Step 5.\n  1081→- **Action:** User clicks \"Back\" twice to Step 3, then \"Next\" twice to Step 5.\n  1082→- **Expected:** All data entered in Steps 3, 4, and 5 is preserved after navigating back and forth. No data is lost.\n  1083→\n  1084→#### Test: Add Listing form works correctly on repeated use\n  1085→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. User has already published one listing successfully.\n  1086→- **Action:** User clicks \"Add Listing\" again, fills out all steps, and publishes.\n  1087→- **Expected:** A second property is created successfully. Both properties appear in the Listings tab. The \"Total Listings\" stat shows the correct total.\n  1088→\n  1089→## Page: User Profile (`/profile`)\n  1090→\n  1091→<!-- Components: ProfileForm, BecomeHostButton, UserReviewsList -->\n  1092→\n  1093→### Component: ProfileForm\n  1094→\n  1095→#### Test: Profile page requires login\n  1096→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n  1097→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1098→- **Expected:** The user is redirected to `/login`. The profile page is not displayed.\n  1099→\n  1100→#### Test: Profile page displays current user info\n  1101→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\", bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\".\n  1102→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1103→- **Expected:** The profile form displays the current values: name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\" (read-only), bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", and avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\". The avatar image is displayed using the URL.\n  1104→\n  1105→#### Test: Edit name field inline\n  1106→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with name \"Alice Smith\".\n  1107→- **Action:** User clicks the name field, clears it, types \"Alice Johnson\", and clicks the \"Save\" button.\n  1108→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated name. The name field displays \"Alice Johnson\". A success message (e.g., \"Profile updated\") is shown. The Redux user state is updated with the new name.\n  1109→\n  1110→#### Test: Edit bio field inline\n  1111→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Love traveling!\".\n  1112→- **Action:** User clicks the bio textarea, clears it, types \"Digital nomad and foodie\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1113→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated bio. The bio field displays \"Digital nomad and foodie\". A success message is shown.\n  1114→\n  1115→#### Test: Edit phone field inline\n  1116→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with phone \"555-1234\".\n  1117→- **Action:** User clicks the phone field, clears it, types \"555-9876\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1118→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated phone. The phone field displays \"555-9876\". A success message is shown.\n  1119→\n  1120→#### Test: Edit avatar URL field inline\n  1121→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with avatar URL \"https://example.com/old-avatar.jpg\".\n  1122→- **Action:** User clicks the avatar URL field, clears it, types \"https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1123→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated avatar URL. The avatar image preview updates to show the new image from \"https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg\". A success message is shown.\n  1124→\n  1125→#### Test: Save with empty name shows validation error\n  1126→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile`.\n  1127→- **Action:** User clears the name field (leaving it empty) and clicks \"Save\".\n  1128→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Name is required\"). No API call is made. The name field is highlighted as invalid.\n  1129→\n  1130→#### Test: Save with invalid avatar URL shows validation error\n  1131→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile`.\n  1132→- **Action:** User enters \"not-a-url\" in the avatar URL field and clicks \"Save\".\n  1133→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid URL\"). No API call is made.\n  1134→\n  1135→#### Test: Profile form fields are functional on repeated edits\n  1136→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with name \"Alice Smith\".\n  1137→- **Action:** User changes the name to \"Alice Johnson\" and clicks \"Save\". After the success message, user changes the name again to \"Alice Williams\" and clicks \"Save\".\n  1138→- **Expected:** Both saves succeed with separate `PUT /api/users/:id` requests. After the second save, the name field displays \"Alice Williams\". Both updates are persisted.\n  1139→\n  1140→#### Test: Email field is displayed but not editable\n  1141→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with email \"alice@example.com\".\n  1142→- **Action:** User views the profile form.\n  1143→- **Expected:** The email \"alice@example.com\" is displayed but the field is read-only / disabled and cannot be edited.\n  1144→\n  1145→#### Test: Profile update persists across navigation\n  1146→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Old bio\".\n  1147→- **Action:** User changes bio to \"New bio\", clicks \"Save\", then navigates to `/` (home page), then navigates back to `/profile`.\n  1148→- **Expected:** The bio field displays \"New bio\", confirming the change was persisted to the database and Redux state.\n  1149→\n  1150→### Component: BecomeHostButton\n  1151→\n  1152→#### Test: Become a Host button is visible for non-host users\n  1153→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false`.\n  1154→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1155→- **Expected:** A \"Become a Host\" button is visible on the profile page.\n  1156→\n  1157→#### Test: Become a Host button is hidden for existing hosts\n  1158→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `true`.\n  1159→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1160→- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is NOT visible on the profile page.\n  1161→\n  1162→#### Test: Clicking Become a Host sets user as host\n  1163→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n  1164→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button.\n  1165→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to become a host?\"). User confirms. A `POST /api/users/:id/become-host` request is sent. Upon success, the button disappears, a success message is shown (e.g., \"You are now a host!\"), and the Redux user state updates `is_host` to `true`. The \"Hosting\" link becomes available in the navigation sidebar.\n  1166→\n  1167→#### Test: Cancel Become a Host confirmation dialog\n  1168→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`. The \"Become a Host\" button is visible.\n  1169→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button, then clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation dialog.\n  1170→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. No API call is made. The \"Become a Host\" button remains visible. `is_host` remains `false`.\n  1171→\n  1172→#### Test: Become a Host button appearance\n  1173→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n  1174→- **Action:** User views the profile page.\n  1175→- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is styled with the coral/red accent color (#FF5A5F), has clear text reading \"Become a Host\", and is visually prominent on the page.\n  1176→\n  1177→### Component: UserReviewsList\n  1178→\n  1179→#### Test: Reviews list displays user's written reviews\n  1180→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written 3 reviews for different properties (e.g., \"Cozy Cabin\" rated 5, \"City Apartment\" rated 3, \"Beach Villa\" rated 4).\n  1181→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1182→- **Expected:** A \"My Reviews\" section is visible showing all 3 reviews. Each review card displays: the property title, the overall rating (with filled/unfilled stars), the comment text, and the date the review was written.\n  1183→\n  1184→#### Test: Reviews list shows empty state for user with no reviews"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pj9Z7o2XYGjwCjrWhWg5SM","session_id":"f2dc69e2-bd3d-45b0-ab90-8317c8b03401","uuid":"2038dec7-9b73-4bc9-aea5-736e9dd9b4fe"}
